## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates knowledge of practical data-structure trade-offs for dynamic ranking. Candidates should justify when to sort on demand vs. maintain auxiliary structures.

## Key Concepts
- Hash map for O(1) key access
- On-demand sorting for top-k retrieval
- Trade-off: simpler updates vs. slower top-k retrieval

## Code Example
```javascript
class CounterTopK {
  constructor() {
    this.counts = new Map(); // key -> count
  }
  add(key, delta) {
    const cur = this.counts.get(key) || 0;
    const next = cur + delta;
    if (next <= 0) this.counts.delete(key); else this.counts.set(key, next);
  }
  get(key) { return this.counts.get(key) || 0; }
  topK(k) {
    const arr = Array.from(this.counts.entries());
    arr.sort((a,b)=> b[1]-a[1] || a[0].localeCompare(b[0]));
    return arr.slice(0,k).map(([key]) => key);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to implement streaming statistics with efficient data structures and real-time median calculation.

## Key Concepts

- Dual heap structure (max-heap + min-heap)
- Balance invariant maintenance
- Median computation in O(log n) per insert
- Streaming data processing

## Code Example

```javascript
class MedianStream {
  constructor() {
    this.low = new MaxHeap();  // Lower half
    this.high = new MinHeap(); // Upper half
  }

  insert(x) {
    // Insert into appropriate heap and rebalance
    if (this.low.isEmpty() || x <= this.low.peek()) {
      this.low.push(x);
    } else {
      this.high.push(x);
    }

    // Rebalance to maintain size difference ≤ 1
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size() + 1) {
      this.high.push(this.low.pop());
    } else if (this.high.size() > this.low.size() + 1) {
      this.low.push(this.high.pop());
    }
  }

  getMedian() {
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size()) {
      return this.low.peek();
    } else if (this.high.size() > this.low.size()) {
      return this.high.peek();
    } else {
      return (this.low.peek() + this.high.peek()) / 2;
    }
  }
}
```

